2. ECGFounder  --  MIT  --  partially bundled
---------------------------------------------
    PKUDigitalHealth / ECGFounder
    https://github.com/PKUDigitalHealth/ECGFounder
    Model weights: https://huggingface.co/PKUDigitalHealth/ECGFounder
    Licence: MIT (code and published weights)

`ecg_pipeline/interpret/net1d.py` is vendored verbatim from ECGFounder.
`ecg_pipeline/interpret/tasks.txt` is the ECGFounder diagnostic class list.
The `.pth` checkpoints are downloaded at setup time and are not stored in git.

MIT is permissive: bundling, modification, and commercial use are allowed provided the
copyright notice and permission notice are retained. Retain them.

Upstream's README says to follow the preprocessing in its `dataset.py`, "including
filtering". Read precisely, upstream has two preprocessing paths and they differ:

  * `ptbxl_eval.py`, the 150-class validation of the pretrained checkpoints, which is
    what this repository uses them for, applies a global z-score
    (`(x - mean) / (std + 1e-8)` over the whole array) and nothing else. No filter.
  * `dataset.py`, the four fine-tuning datasets, first applies `util.filter_bandpass`:
    a 50 Hz notch (Q=30) and a 4th-order Butterworth bandpass at 0.67-40 Hz, then the
    same z-score.

`waveform.zscore` is the z-score, applied as `ptbxl_eval.py` applies it. No filter is
applied, matching the evaluation path rather than the fine-tuning one. Whether the
bandpass helps or hurts on a digitized paper ECG is measurable and has not been
measured; `scripts/derive_thresholds_colab.ipynb` runs both variants on PTB-XL.


